{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1208","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Bits And Pieces"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ integers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You need to find the maximum value of $$$a_{i} | ( a_{j} \\& a_{k} )$$$ over all triplets $$$(i,j,k)$$$ such that $$$i \\lt j \\lt k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here $$$\\&$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#AND"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise AND operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", and $$$|$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#OR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise OR operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains the integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 10^{6}$$$), the size of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next line contains $$$n$$$ space separated integers $$$a_1$$$, $$$a_2$$$, ..., $$$a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_{i} \\le 2 \\cdot 10^{6}$$$), representing the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer, the maximum value of the expression given in the statement. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n2 4 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n2 8 4 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n12\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the only possible triplet is $$$(1, 2, 3)$$$. Hence, the answer is $$$2 | (4 \\& 6) = 6$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, there are $$$4$$$ possible triplets: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(1, 2, 3)$$$, value of which is $$$2|(8\\&4) = 2$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(1, 2, 4)$$$, value of which is $$$2|(8\\&7) = 2$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(1, 3, 4)$$$, value of which is $$$2|(4\\&7) = 6$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(2, 3, 4)$$$, value of which is $$$8|(4\\&7) = 12$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The maximum value hence is $$$12$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1208F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1208/problem/F"}